# Playwright Locators

Never use absolute XPath. Prefer Playwright’s built-in locators, in this order:

1. `getByRole`
2. `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` / `getByText`
3. `getByTestId`
4. `getByAltText` / `getByTitle`
5. CSS via `page.locator(...)` only when the above cannot express the target

## Forbidden

```typescript
// ❌ Absolute XPath
page.locator('xpath=/html/body/div[1]/form/button[2]')
page.locator('//*[@id="root"]/div/div[3]/button')
page.$x('/html/body/...')
```

## Required

```typescript
// ✅ Role / label / test id
page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Submit' })
page.getByLabel('Email')
page.getByTestId('checkout-submit')

// ✅ Scoped CSS (relative, intentional) when needed
page.locator('[data-qa="cart"] .line-item')
```

Relative XPath (`xpath=//button[@type="submit"]`) is a last resort only when no Playwright locator or stable CSS exists — never absolute paths from `/html` or `/body`.
